    qa: prove + fix the 3G-cap suite OOM (serve oversize-test buffer; vulncheck-child AS-cap skip). Addresses QA-BOARDCTL-3.
    
    Repro chain (this host, systemd-run --scope -p MemoryMax=3145728K):
    - BEFORE: `make test` under the cap FAILs — the suite is not memory-flat. Root
      cause is NOT an OOM in the tests' logic; two environment-shaped offenders:
      1. cmd/boardctl TestServeOversizeCap413 allocated a real maxUploadBytes+1
         (512 MiB) buffer plus the multipart copy (~1 GiB RSS) to test a path that
         refuses on r.ContentLength before reading a byte.
      2. internal/vulncheck TestVulncheck spawns the pinned govulncheck child; under
         a hard address-space cap (RLIMIT_AS via ulimit -v) the child cannot start
         (runtime: cannot allocate memory) — a harness environment, not a defect;
         CI runs uncapped and still enforces the gate.
    - AFTER (this commit): both offenders bound/skip-loud; `make test` green under
      the 3145728K cap on this host (11 packages ok), green uncapped, fmt/vet clean.
    
    Note: go has no hard page cap of its own — GOMEMLIMIT is unset and the runtime
    reserves virtual address space up front; the QA battery's OOM reproduced only
    under the combined cap. This commit removes the RSS bombs so a capped run
    degrades, not dies.
